    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`) passes. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for owners. When a request includes `birthDate` (ISO), the owner response now returns `ageBand` computed against `registrationDate`: `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+); it's absent when no `birthDate` is supplied.\n\nChanges, following the codebase's existing conventions:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the editable `OwnerFields` schema, and `ageBand` as a read-only derived string on the `Owner` schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time and MapStruct auto-maps them by name (matching how `contactPreference`, `membershipLevel`, etc. already work). I deliberately kept `ageBand` a plain string rather than an OpenAPI `enum` to avoid a generated enum type that would break the MapStruct `String`\u2192enum mapping from the derived getter.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persistent `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with accessors, plus a derived `getAgeBand()` method that computes the band from `birthDate` against `registrationDate` (falling back to today only if `registrationDate` is somehow unset), mirroring the style of the other derived getters like `getContactPreference()`.\n- **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the extra `NULL` to each positional owners INSERT so column counts still match (the h2/postgres seed data use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nThe registration flow required no controller changes: the `birthDate` input flows through the existing `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` mapping, and `registrationDate` is already resolved before save, so `getAgeBand()` reads a populated reference date on both create and read.",
